func knapsack(wt, val, cap) =
  {
    {
      local n = wt.listLen()
      local dp = []
      for (i: 1 .. cap + 1 step 1) {
        dp.add(0)
      }
      for (i: 1 .. n step 1) {
        for (w: cap + 1 .. 1 step -1) {
          if (wt[i] <= w - 1) {
            local test = dp[w - wt[i]] + val[i]
            if (test > dp[w]) {
              dp[w] = test
            }
          }
        }
      }
      dp[cap + 1]
    }
  }

1. Define knapsack(wt, val, cap): 0/1 knapsack using 1D DP array.
2. Initialize dp list of size cap+1 with zeros.
3. For each item i, iterate w from cap down to wt[i].
4. Update dp[w] if including item improves value.
5. Return dp[cap+1].

