func mergeSort(list) =
  {
    if (list.listLen() <= 1) {
      list
    } else {
      local mid = floor(list.listLen() / 2)
      local left = mergeSort(list.slice(1, mid))
      local right = mergeSort(list.slice(mid + 1, list.listLen()))
      local res = []
      local i = 1
      local j = 1
      while (i <= left.listLen() && j <= right.listLen()) {
        if (left[i] < right[j]) {
          res.add(left[i])
          i = i + 1
        } else {
          res.add(right[j])
          j = j + 1
        }
      }
      while (i <= left.listLen()) {
        res.add(left[i])
        i = i + 1
      }
      while (j <= right.listLen()) {
        res.add(right[j])
        j = j + 1
      }
      res
    }
  }

Goal: Sort a list using merge sort — a divide and conquer algorithm.

1. Base case: if the list has 1 or fewer elements, it's already sorted — return it.
2. Find mid = floor(listLen / 2) — split point.
3. Recursively sort the left half: slice(1, mid).
4. Recursively sort the right half: slice(mid + 1, listLen).
5. Merge the two sorted halves:
   - Use pointers i and j starting at 1 for each half.
   - Compare left[i] and right[j], take the smaller, advance that pointer.
   - Continue until one half is exhausted.
6. Append any remaining elements from the unfinished half.
7. Return the merged sorted list.

