2. Base case: list of 1 or fewer elements has 0 inversions.
3. Split into left and right halves, recursively count inversions in each.
4. Merge the two sorted halves:
   - When we take an element from the RIGHT half instead of the left, every remaining element in the LEFT half forms an inversion with it.
   - So add (lSorted.listLen() - i + 1) to inv each time we take from right.
5. Return [merged sorted list, total inversion count].
